      "text": [
        ": سَأَلْتُ أَبَا جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنِ اَلْمُعْتَكِفِ يُجَامِعُ قَالَ «إِذَا فَعَلَ ذَلِكَ فَعَلَيْهِ مَا عَلَى اَلْمُظَاهِرِ ».\nوَ قَدْ رُوِيَ: «أَنَّهُ إِنْ جَامَعَ فِي اَللَّيْلِ فَعَلَيْهِ كَفَّارَةٌ وَاحِدَةٌ وَ إِنْ جَامَعَ بِالنَّهَارِ فَعَلَيْهِ كَفَّارَتَانِ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.2102 - It is narrated by Al-Hasan ibn Mahbub, from Ali ibn Ri'ab, from Zurara, who said:\n\"I asked Abu Ja'far (as) about the ruling on an individual performing i'tikaf who engages in sexual relations.\nImam (as) said: 'If they do so, they incur the same penalty as one who has taken a vow of zihar (atonement).'\"\nIt has also been narrated: \"If they engage in sexual relations during the night, they must pay one expiation. However, if they engage in sexual relations during the day, they must pay two expiations.\""
        ]
      }
    },
